{#
    One question, and the blocks folded behind it.

    The question is a property because it fits in one. The answer is between
    the tags because a paragraph, a list and a code block are not what an
    attribute carries. The directive handed down which set it folds in, as a
    renderer has no upgrade in which the set can hand it down itself.

    The page's address for one answer arrives as `anchor` and lands on the
    answer. The platform opens a fold where a fragment points into it, and
    leaves one shut where it points at it. The set is `group` here and `name`
    on the element, as the address already takes `name` on a node.
#}
<sds-accordion-item
    question="{{ node.option('question') }}"
    {%- if node.option('group') %} name="{{ node.option('group') }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if node.option('anchor') %} anchor="{{ node.option('anchor') }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if node.option('open') %} open{% endif %}
    {%- if node.option('class') %} class="{{ node.option('class') }}"{% endif %}>
    {%- for child in node.children -%}
        {{ renderNode(child) }}
    {%- endfor -%}
</sds-accordion-item>
